<title>USA: TABLE- Keystone Q2 $0.29/shr vs $0.43.</title>
<headline>TABLE- Keystone Q2 $0.29/shr vs $0.43.</headline>
<dateline>HARRISBURG, Pa. 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Keystone Financial Inc</p>
<p>Financial Highlights (Unaudited)</p>
<p>	    For the three months ended For the six months ended</p>
<p>			6/30/97     6/30/96     6/30/97     6/30/96</p>
<p> Net income	 $14,982     $22,769     $37,753     $44,430</p>
<p> Earnings per share  0.29	  0.43	  0.73	 0 .85</p>
<p>Excluding special charges</p>
<p>and investment losses:</p>
<p> Earnings per share  0.46	 0 .43	  0.90	  0.85</p>
<p>Average shares</p>
<p>  outstanding	51,320	 52,116	51,475     52,079</p>
<p>(All numbers in 000s, except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: The bank said the second-quarter 1997 results include special charges totaling $8.7 million, or $0.17 a share. The charges related to the bank's takeover of Financial Trust Co May 30 and a $0.5 million investment securities loss because of portfolio restructuring.</p>
<p>The bank's asssets totaled $6.88 billion at the end of the second quarter, compared with $6.21 billion a year ago. The bank's full name is Keystone Financial Inc.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
